{"id":"festival-marketplace","title":"Festival Marketplace","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Festival_Marketplace","rev":240059,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Festival Marketplace"]}," is an architectural and graphic aesthetic popular during the mid-1980s to mid-1990s. It takes inspiration from 1800s-1900s shopping vernacular with a Postmodern interpretation and updated in a simplified, colourful, celebratory form. This aesthetic was primarily seen used in shopping malls, food courts, and grocery stores."]}],"sections":[{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Serif fonts"]},{"c":["Grid motifs"]},{"c":["Checkerboard patterns"]},{"c":["Diamond shapes"]},{"c":["Flags, ribbons, & balloons"]},{"c":["Arches, fountains, glass roofs, & indoor awnings"]},{"c":["Patterned tiles"]},{"c":["Large, colorful shop-like signs marking store sections"]},{"c":["Circular logos"]}]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Brands"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Claires"]},{"c":["Chucky Cheese"]},{"c":["Revolve"]},{"c":["Jaded London"]},{"c":["Spencers"]},{"c":["Rosa Bloom"]},{"c":["Faneuil Hall Marketplace (Boston)"]},{"c":["Harborplace (Baltimore)"]},{"c":["Bayside Marketplace (Miami)"]},{"c":["Joinus Handbags"]},{"c":["JMC Hairwear"]},{"c":["H&M"]},{"c":["American Eagle"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Places"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Hillsboro Antique Mall"]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/eb/FM_The_Food_Fair.webp/revision/latest?cb=20260406234120","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Southland Mall,"]}," Hayward, CA, USA (1988)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/7/74/FM_Trackside.webp/revision/latest?cb=20260406233946","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Indianapolis Union Station Mall"]},", Indianapolis, IN, USA (1984)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthe